{"type":"text","timestamp":1787411395828,"sessionID":"ses_fd5fb554dffeZja3DG2pTz3720","part":{"id":"prt_02a056b17001ratQNtBRVqqURs","messageID":"msg_02a054e7e001UqtlQyAYwtSzsl","sessionID":"ses_fd5fb554dffeZja3DG2pTz3720","type":"text","text":"The 5 test failures are pre-existing (present without my change) and unrelated to caching — they're bugs in the range-matching logic the test asserts.\n\nMy change to `internal/lrucache.js` implements a real bounded LRU:\n- `get` moves the key to most-recently-used\n- `set` moves existing keys to MRU and evicts the LRU key when at `max`\n- `set` still ignores `undefined` values and returns `this`\n- `delete` returns presence as before\n\nVerified: after 1500 inserts size stays at 1000, oldest keys evicted, MRU preserved, and undefined values aren't stored. Library output is unchanged since a cache miss just recomputes the same result.","time":{"start":1787411393303,"end":1787411395822}}}
